  type_set_err_inline.pcpp - break step of type_set.pcpp:
  a set type is declared in a type block and used by its name (PR0026)

  How to check, from repo\bin:
    pcpp res\tests\type_set_err_inline.pcpp
    pcpp res\tests\type_set_err_inline.pcpp -t x86_64-linux-gnu
  The marked line reports that code; nothing else is reported.
*******************************************************************************/

module exe type_set_err_inline;

var
  LS: set of 0..15; // ERROR PR0026@7: a 'set of' type is declared in a type block (type TName = ...;) and used by its name

begin
end.
